{"id": "z1089", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most likely place to find an emer ald in the eastern United States is probably a flower bed. However, it's important to clarify that we' re talking about the gemstone em erald here, not the marine creature. Emerald s are typically found in alluvial deposits or within specific types of rock formations like ze olite veins. While these mineral-rich area s might be hidden beneath the soil in places like certain parts of Florida or even the Appalachian region, you wouldn't see them naturally growing in a tide pool or coral reefs since those environments don' t host emeralds. A quariums display various marine life but not gemstones. So if you're looking for an emerald in the eastern U.S., your best chance would be exploring areas known for gem mining or checking out geological sites where such minerals could be present.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1097", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "John needed a straight wire. Unfortunately, this one had endured some abuse and had become what? A bent, B bent, C crook ed, D straight forth, E curved.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
