{"id": "z1113", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A hemispher e experiences summer when it' s angled towards the largest star in the solar system. So, C is correct.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1121", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A star burning far away has enormous pressure and temperature, but that doesn't directly affect things on Earth. So let's look at the options. A room having overhead lights is something we control ourselves, not related to a distant star. Night on Earth being dimly lit is actually caused by our own moon reflecting sunlight, so it ’s not really affected by distant stars. Plastic stars to decorate a ceiling are just decoration s we make here. And finally, a person being the star of a show is about performance, not science. So none of these options are correct based on how stars work in reality.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1129", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, the Arctic. Seals are well adapted to cold environment s and are often found in the polar regions, such as the Arctic and Antarctic.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1137", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The ice cube will shrink as it absorb s the heat from the sun. So the correct answer is A, sh rink.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1145", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When you're trying to pull a rose out of the ground, you encounter resistance because of its root s. The roots anchor the plant in the soil, making it difficult to pull up without digging or using tools.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1153", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The winter solstice is on December 2 1st in the southern hemisphere. So, the answer is D.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
