{"id": "z1169", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There is a heighten ed threat of lands lide in B, the And es. The Andes are mountain s that run through several South American countries, and they have steep slopes, heavy rain, and sometimes earthquakes, all of which make landslides more likely. The desert has very little water, so landslides are rare there. The ocean doesn't have land to slide down, and Indiana is flat with fewer steep areas where lands lides happen easily. So the best answer is B, the Andes.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
