{"id": "z1185", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The harder a child pushes a toy car, B, the further it will roll across the floor.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1193", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A. An organism that makes food for itself is nutrition ally self- sustaining. This means it can produce its own energy and nutrients through processes like photosynthesis or chemosynthesis, so it doesn't need to rely on other organisms for food.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1201", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Objects used to hold sheets of paper together are often ferromag netic. These are typically clips or fast eners that use magnetism to keep papers aligned in binders or folders. While some might be wooden or electronic, the most common type for this purpose is fer romagnetic.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1209", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A rabbit has a litter of bunnies. Most of the babies are white, just like the mother ra bbit, but one baby has brown spot s like the father ra bbit. The father rabbit pass es down inherited characteristics. So even though most of the kit s look like their mom with white fur, that little bunny with brown spots got those color traits from dad. It' s how genetic information is passed from parents to kids.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1217", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, water can be found in its gas form, also known as steam or vapor. It is most likely to be present inside of a brass pipe because pipes are often used for carrying hot water and producing steam. Water might also exist in the atmosphere a mile up in the sky where it forms clouds before falling back down as rain or snow. However, you wouldn't find gas water inside a leather baseball since ball s aren't designed to hold gases.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1225", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, polar bears are usually white to blend in with the snow and ice. So it would be C, blending in.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1233", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best method for detecting texture is B, seeing it. While touch ing something can give you a sense of its surface, seeing allows us to observe patterns, rough ness, and other visual cues that help identify the texture directly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1241", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C, cat and catfish. Cat s reproduce sexually like most animals, while catfish lay eggs or give birth to live young depending on the species. So they don't reproduce in the same way.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1249", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B. Humans pre date fossil fuel formation. Fos sil fuels like coal, oil, and natural gas formed over millions of years from ancient plants and organisms buried deep underground. Human s evolved much later than these deposit s were formed, so they existed in the ground long before humans appeared on Earth.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1257", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The dashboard reading in a Ja guar would likely be set to kilometers. So the answer is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1265", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A diabetic would need to be careful with a. bro ccoli, as it contains natural sugar. While broccoli is generally low in carbo hydrates, diabe tics should still monitor portion sizes and overall intake of starchy vegetables. The other options are not primarily made of sugar. Meat has no sugar, cell ery has minimal sugar content, and toast does contain car bohydrates but usually from fl our rather than added sugar. So the best answer is a. brocc oli.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1273", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When a substance touches something cold, it usually cools down if it's warmer than the object. So among your options, warm is the most likely to cool when it comes into contact with a cold surface. That’s because heat flows from warmer things to colder ones. If you touch a cold object with warm stuff like water or air, it lose s heat and gets cooler. F rozen or chill y things are already cold, so they don’t cool much more. Col d stuff stays cold unless it meets something even colder. So the best answer is warm.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
