{"id": "z1809", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Rebecca has 9 eggs, and she wants to split them into groups of three. If we divide nine by three, that gives us three groups. The bananas and marble s are not relevant for this calculation since the question is only about the eggs. So there will be three groups created.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1817", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "At the arcade Dave had won seven tickets. He used some tickets to buy toys. If he still has two tickets left, how many tickets did Dave use to buy toys?", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1825", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are 11 different books and 17 different movies in the Crazy Silly School series. If you read 7 of the books, that means you have read 7 books. And if you watched 21 of the movies, that means you have watched 21 movies. To find out how many more movies than books you have read, we need to subtract the number of books from the number of movies. So, 21 movies minus 7 books equals 14. Therefore, you have watched 14 more movies than books.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 35, "carrier_ended": null}
