{"id": "z1841", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "For the walls of the house, John would use 1 1 nails in total. Each plank needs three pieces of nail s to be secured, and there's an additional eight nail s used for some reason. So if we subtract those extra eight nail s from the total, that leaves us with three nails actually being used per pl ank. Since each plank requires three nails, he only needs one plank for the wall.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1849", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first chapter has 9 1 pages and the second chapter has 2 3 pages. To find out how many more pages the first chapter has than the second, you subtract the number of pages in the second chapter from the first. So, 9 1 minus 23 equal s 68. Therefore, the first chapter has 6 8 more pages than the second chapter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1857", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are eight different movies in the series. If you watched four of them, then there are still four more that you haven' t seen yet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1865", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, if they fill 22 1 drum s of grapes each day, then over 7 7 days, they would fill about 16, 9 37 drum s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1873", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The school has 67 classrooms and each classroom has 6 6 students. So first we need to figure out how many students are going on the field trip. If you multi ply 6 7 by 6 6, that gives us a total of 4 422 students. Now each bus can hold 6 seat s. To find out how many buses are needed, we divide the total number of students by the capacity of each bus. So 4 4 22 divided by 6 is about 73 7. But since you can't have a fraction of a bus, we round up to the next whole number. That means they will need 7 40 buses for the trip.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 38, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1881", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Danny lost 66 bottle caps at the park. Now he has 25 left in his collection. To find out how many he had to begin with, we need to add the ones he lost back to the ones he still has. So that's 6 6 plus 2 5. Let' s do the math: 60 plus 20 is 80, and 6 plus 5 is 11. Add ing those together gives us 9 1. That means Danny originally had 9 1 bottle caps in his collection.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1889", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The machine makes 3 shirts per minute. If it made 6 shirt s in total, we divide the total number of shirt s by the rate to find the time. So, 6 divided by 3 equals 2. The machine was working for 2 minutes.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
